From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the shader set converts the recipe's compute records too (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 (exact "1", read once). Needs EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1 (and so
EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1). Off: nothing changes (the same records, the same file bytes, the same
stamp).

Why: the d4 cold start (13 Nov) converted 113,054 of the recipe's 120,461 records and dropped all
4,088 compute records ("dropped compute-predicted-unsupported: 4088"). That was by design, not a
missing key part: the first port lowered only vertex and pixel programs ("No compute/mesh
guesses", Lower) and dropped every kind-1 record before looking at it. In that start the game
asked for 94 compute pipelines (first_start.list, C rows), every one translated on the GPU thread.

What, with the switch:
- Lower() also lowers compute programs (stage 5): from the code area's first byte, with a zero
  program header in front, as ComputeEnvironment does for a native program (source header size
  0; the live hash is CityHash64 of that code ^ 0x4f554e4345000003, the same tag). GUESS, not
  checked on the game's files: that the extractor's compute code area starts with the first
  instruction (the extractor takes the stage from the control section, not from a header). If it
  does not, these programs fail to lower or never meet a live key: the drop line and the 0781
  counts say so, and nothing else changes.
- A compute record (one fact, recipe kind 1) is written with its key as the bytes of
  ComputePipelineCacheKey: the lowered hash, the shared memory size and the workgroup size, the
  last two from the fact's last 16 bytes (FileEnvironment::Serialize order: workgroup x, y, z,
  shared). Checks: fingerprint found, lowered, and the fact as the live compute environment
  serializes it (start address 80, lowest read 0, stage 5, the texture bank the lowering needs).
  Drop reasons as for graphics.
- Compute facts are stored whole (tables, then workgroup and shared memory); AppendEnvironment
  adds no program header after a compute fact (Deserialize reads the 16 bytes instead).
- ReadRecords gets an optional on_compute callback. A record with a 24-byte key goes to it and
  nowhere else; readers without it (the preparation without 0781, the WHY catalogue) skip compute
  records, and key_wanted is never asked about them.
- The stamp gets the line "compute 1", so a set made without the switch is converted again once
  (and back when it is turned off). One more log line: how many converted records are compute.

Measured on the Mac (t158/recipe_check.py, our notes): the 94 C rows of the d4 list all have a
record in this console's own backed-up vulkan.bin files, so compute keys repeat across sessions;
87 of them have a recipe compute record with the same answers (handle values aside), workgroup
and shared memory (50 with the same lowered length in Fritchii's file). INFERRED: those are the
same programs; only the console run can prove the keys meet.

T161s: applies after 0770-0772 (T157); the code is T158's, only the context lines are new.
